From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tui_gateway: the legacy hand-back uses the gateway
 claim's own predicate; its owner answer is one state.db open per chat per
 poll

Review 5887848770 (t_01a1d3ddaceef7fd) on PR #1720, both nits:

1. The legacy poller handed a chat back on ledger/lease alone. The gateway's
   tui-owner claim (owned_live_session) also needs a live LOCAL adapter and an
   authority for the row's notifier_profile. With forwardable ledger work on a
   profile the gateway does not serve, or with no live gateway at all, nobody
   claimed until the ledger work ended. Now the chat-level half requires the
   verified live default gateway (pid from gateway.status) and, for the lease,
   that gateway's pid; the row-level half (claims_row) mirrors
   _launch_authority (unstamped or the gateway's launch profile, from its
   served_profiles record) and skips threaded rows. The board poll skips only
   rows the gateway claims; the buffered hand-back fires only when every claim
   is one it claims. Each owner change is logged once at INFO (episode start /
   back with this backend).
2. _kb_gateway_owns ran on every 5 s poll for every live chat, twice when
   something was pending, opening state.db once per lineage id. The answer is
   now memoized per chat for OWNER_TTL_S (5 s, the poll interval) and a fresh
   one reads the ledger and turn leases over the whole lineage in one open.

Tests (tests/gateway/test_kanban_tui_sibling_custody.py): (a) forwardable
ledger work on an unserved profile and (b) forwardable ledger work with no
live gateway / LOCAL adapter both keep the chat with the legacy leg, claimed
once, never handed back, nothing else delivers it; the INFO episode logs once
per change; N=24 polls x M=3 chats with 3-id lineages open state.db at most
once per chat per TTL.
